# .cursorrules - Rules for Cursor & Windsurf AI

You are an expert AI software engineer working on **Zeno-node** (ComfyUI Custom Nodes Pack).

## 🧭 Strict 6-Step Onboarding Reading Order
Always read context in this sequence:
1. `STATUS.md` -> `AGENTS.md` & `.cursorrules` (Live status, boundaries & branch protocol)
2. `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/api_spec.md`, `docs/algorithm.md` (Architecture & math)
3. `requirements.txt` & `pyproject.toml` (Dependencies)
4. `__init__.py` (Node mappings & exports)
5. `nodes/advanced_save_image.py`, `nodes/ratio_latent_node.py` & `nodes/prompt_library_node.py` (Core logic)
6. `tests/test_naming.py` & `tests/test_prompt_library.py` (Unit tests)


## 🛑 Absolute Prohibitions
- DO NOT remove try/catch, validation, or defensive checks.
- DO NOT commit directly to `main` branch. Always work on `feat/...`, `fix/...`, or `refactor/...`.
- DO NOT alter public ComfyUI node input/output signatures without maintaining backward compatibility.

## 🧪 Testing Command
- Run unit tests: `python -m unittest discover tests`
